{
  "_comment": [
    "The Traditional Chinese terminology and register lock.",
    "",
    "This is the file to edit, NOT the prompt templates. It is injected into",
    "every prompt AND used to audit every answer, so a change here moves both",
    "what the model is told and what it is checked against.",
    "",
    "Parallel in purpose to llm/zh/data/termbase_zh.json (Simplified) and",
    "llm/vi/data/termbase.json (Vietnamese). Written for older Traditional",
    "Chinese-speaking adults in Australia, largely Taiwan and Hong Kong",
    "background: Traditional characters, Taiwan-register vocabulary, and",
    "the respectful second person.",
    "",
    "Generated from termbase_zh.json via OpenCC (s2twp: Simplified to",
    "Traditional, Taiwan phrasing), then hand-reviewed. A character-only",
    "conversion is not enough on its own -- some terms differ in the word",
    "chosen, not just the script (e.g. mainland 手机/网络/短信 vs Taiwan",
    "手機/網路/簡訊), which is exactly what s2twp corrects for."
  ],
  "register": {
    "_why": [
      "Chinese has no neutral second person. Addressing an older adult as 你",
      "is not informal, it is disrespectful -- and 你 is what every model",
      "reaches for, because it is what web copy uses and web copy is written",
      "for thirty-year-olds. Same class of problem as bạn vs ông/bà in the",
      "Vietnamese lane: a correctness bug, not a style preference.",
      "",
      "Enforced twice: stated in the prompt, and audited after generation.",
      "Telling a model not to do something is not the same as it not doing it."
    ],
    "required_address": "您",
    "self_reference": "我們",
    "forbidden": [
      {
        "form": "你",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Familiar second person. Use 您 for an older reader."
      },
      {
        "form": "你們",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Familiar plural. Use 您 or 兩位."
      },
      {
        "form": "親",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "E-commerce familiarity. Never to a senior."
      },
      {
        "form": "喂",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Abrupt call-out. Reads as rude in writing."
      },
      {
        "form": "哥們",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Slang address."
      },
      {
        "form": "老人家",
        "severity": "warn",
        "note": "Can read as patronising in instructions. Prefer 您."
      }
    ]
  },
